      "explanation": "<p>PhSNa replaces F from o- and p-dinitro- fluorobenzene\nvia nucleophilic aromatic substitution.</p>\n<p>PhSNa replaces Cl from compound D via nucleophilic\nbimolecular substitution reaction.</p>\n<p>In case of compound B and C, nucleophilic substitution is not\npossible neither by S<sub>N</sub>Ar or S<sub>N</sub>2 . because, the electron\nwithdrawing group is present at meta-position and halogen is\nattached to sp<sup>2</sup>-carbon.</p>\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kx89yrec/8db4b5e2-8f47-4754-8548-91c4e1906dbb/35daaf40-5e0e-11ec-b6f3-d95f9331133d/file-1kx89yred.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kx89yrec/8db4b5e2-8f47-4754-8548-91c4e1906dbb/35daaf40-5e0e-11ec-b6f3-d95f9331133d/file-1kx89yred.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2021 Paper 1 Online Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 34 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1kx89yrec/8db4b5e2-8f47-4754-8548-91c4e1906dbb/35daaf40-5e0e-11ec-b6f3-d95f9331133d/file-1kx89yred.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1kx89yrec/8db4b5e2-8f47-4754-8548-91c4e1906dbb/35daaf40-5e0e-11ec-b6f3-d95f9331133d/file-1kx89yred.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kx89yrec/8db4b5e2-8f47-4754-8548-91c4e1906dbb/35daaf40-5e0e-11ec-b6f3-d95f9331133d/file-1kx89yred.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1kx89yrec/8db4b5e2-8f47-4754-8548-91c4e1906dbb/35daaf40-5e0e-11ec-b6f3-d95f9331133d/file-1kx89yred.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1kx89yrec/8db4b5e2-8f47-4754-8548-91c4e1906dbb/35daaf40-5e0e-11ec-b6f3-d95f9331133d/file-1kx89yred.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1kx89yrec/8db4b5e2-8f47-4754-8548-91c4e1906dbb/35daaf4